<p>This policy explains how Krujim Inc, doing business as Koast ("Koast," "we," "us"), handles personal information through our website, Rider app, Driver app, Connect operator software and related support and communications. It covers riders and bookers, passengers, chauffeurs, transportation-company owners and staff, and website visitors. If you use more than one product or role, the relevant sections apply together.</p>
<p>Our transportation service and our software platform serve different purposes. For a ride provided by Koast, Krujim Inc handles information as the transportation operator. When another transportation company uses our software, that company determines how it manages its own reservations, workforce and customer records. Koast processes those records to provide its software and also handles information for its own account security, support and business purposes. The other company's privacy notice may also apply. Contact us if you need help identifying the company responsible for a reservation or record.</p>

<h2 id="information">1. Information we collect</h2>
<p><strong>Information you or an authorized person provides.</strong> This may include your name, contact details, account and profile information, photograph, saved places, preferences, passengers, emergency contacts, reservation instructions, messages, support requests, documents and payment-related information. A booker, employer, dispatcher or transportation operator may provide information about a passenger or chauffeur. Provide another person's information only when you have the appropriate authority and have given them any required notice.</p>
<p><strong>Information from using the services.</strong> We process reservation and trip activity, pickup and destination information, flight details, transaction and receipt records, communications and delivery status, location where enabled, and security and technical information such as IP address, browser description, sign-in times and recorded activity. Browser descriptions are approximate and do not uniquely identify a physical device.</p>
<p><strong>Connected services.</strong> If you choose a connected service, we receive the information needed for the feature you authorize. Examples include Google sign-in, Calendar, payment processing, maps and flight information. Connecting one feature does not make unrelated account information available to everyone using Koast.</p>
<p><strong>Payments.</strong> Card-entry features use the payment processor's card components. Koast stores payment references and limited details such as card brand and last four digits to recognize a saved method and process authorized transactions. Saved methods are associated with the relevant customer and operator.</p>

<h2 id="riders">2. Riders, bookers and passengers</h2>
<p>We use rider and passenger information to provide quotes, arrange and fulfill reservations, identify the correct passengers, coordinate pickup, process authorized payments, provide receipts and support, and apply the preferences you supply. Saved places and accessibility or comfort instructions may reveal sensitive information; include only what is useful for your service.</p>
<p><strong>Your device location.</strong> If you enable Rider location features and grant device permission, we can use precise location for map and pickup assistance. During supported pickup stages, rider coordinates may be shared with the assigned chauffeur and dispatch to help locate the passenger. You can turn the app location setting or device permission off. A typed pickup address and a chauffeur's location updates are separate sources of trip-location information.</p>
<p>For a reservation, the responsible operator and assigned chauffeur receive the information needed to fulfill it, such as passenger name and contact information, pickup and destination, flight information, luggage and relevant trip instructions. A person or company booking for you may receive reservation information needed to manage that booking. Sharing a ride link or inviting a safety contact makes the information shown by that feature available to the recipient; share links only with people you trust.</p>
<p><strong>Operator boundaries.</strong> Using Koast does not give every operator access to your entire account. Operator customer records, private notes, ride and payment history, saved payment methods and favorite-chauffeur relationships are kept within the relevant organization. Information needed to fulfill a particular reservation may be provided to its fulfilling operator. Reusable profile sharing across additional operators is a planned feature, not a currently available control. Before enabling it, we will explain its scope and provide a separate choice; signing in is not consent to that future sharing.</p>

<h2 id="drivers">3. Chauffeurs and the Driver app</h2>
<p>We process chauffeur identity and contact information, profile and availability information, organization relationships, assigned trips and trip-status updates, communications, and documents supplied for licensing, insurance, vehicle or compliance review. An operator or authorized administrator may supply or review records relevant to its operations. Use of the app does not determine whether you are an employee or an independent contractor.</p>
<p><strong>Location.</strong> When location tracking is enabled, the Driver app can send precise coordinates and related trip-status information to support dispatch, ETA calculation and ride tracking. Tracking associated with accepted work may include garage positioning before passenger pickup and return travel after dropoff, depending on the trip and operator settings. Relevant location information is made available to authorized dispatch staff and, where the ride-tracking feature applies, to the rider. Collection is not limited to the time a passenger is inside the vehicle.</p>
<p>You can use the app's tracking control and your device's location permissions to stop device-location collection. Doing so affects tracking and availability features. Browser, operating-system and connectivity limits can interrupt updates, including while the app is in the background; the feature is not a guarantee of continuous monitoring. Previously recorded trip and location information is not erased merely by turning tracking off.</p>

<h2 id="operators">4. Operators and Connect</h2>
<p>Connect processes business and staff contact details, roles and access settings, customer and passenger records, reservations, vehicles, chauffeur and compliance records, pricing and policy settings, payment references, messages, documents, reports and activity records supplied through the software. Authorized staff see information according to their organization and permissions. Koast administrators may access relevant records for authorized support, safety, security and platform administration.</p>
<p>An operator is responsible for its own workforce and customer notices, lawful instructions and user access. Koast's software does not transfer ownership of an operator-originated customer relationship to another operator. Requests about records controlled by an operator may need that operator's involvement; we will help route a request where appropriate. Any separately agreed data-processing terms also apply to the relevant business service.</p>

<h2 id="location-recordings-ai">5. Optional permissions, safety recordings and AI</h2>
<p><strong>Device permissions.</strong> Features such as using your current location, uploading a photo, recording audio, voice input and push notifications may require browser or device permission. Granting one permission does not grant all others. You can change device permissions, although a feature may stop working. Denying microphone access does not cancel a reservation.</p>
<p><strong>Ride audio.</strong> The optional ride-recording feature records audio. Use it only after obtaining the participant agreement required by the feature and any consent required by law. With that agreement, audio is encrypted on the recording device and automatically uploaded to Koast. Authorized Koast owner reviewers may listen for safety or service review even when no incident report has been filed. Either participant can withdraw to stop further recording; already uploaded audio remains until scheduled deletion. The feature provides a seven-day access window and scheduled cleanup. A separately preserved incident or legal record may need to be retained for its applicable purpose. Recording is not continuously monitored and is not an emergency response service.</p>
<p><strong>AI features.</strong> When you use Concierge, Kopilot or other AI-assisted features, relevant messages, attachments and account or reservation context may be processed by our AI service providers, including OpenAI, to answer questions or carry out supported actions. Document-assistance features may process uploaded licensing or compliance documents. Do not submit unrelated sensitive information. AI output can be incorrect; verify important information and contact a person for help with service or safety issues.</p>

<h2 id="purposes">6. Why we use information</h2>
<p>We use information to provide and support the requested service; authenticate users and protect accounts; coordinate transportation and communications; process authorized payments and maintain business records; administer operator access; prevent fraud, abuse and security incidents; investigate safety or service issues; diagnose and improve our products; and comply with applicable obligations. Optional marketing communications are subject to the choices and consent requirements that apply to them. Sign-in or acceptance of terms is not consent to promotional text messages, optional recordings or future profile sharing.</p>

<h2 id="sharing">7. Who receives information</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>People involved in your service:</strong> authorized bookers, the responsible operator, assigned chauffeurs and recipients you choose, to the extent needed for their role or the feature you use.</li>
<li><strong>Service providers:</strong> infrastructure and storage providers such as Cloudflare; payment providers such as Stripe; communications providers such as Twilio and email or push-delivery services; Google for connected features and abuse prevention; AI providers such as OpenAI; and maps, flight and support services, as needed for the feature.</li>
<li><strong>Legal and safety recipients:</strong> appropriate recipients where disclosure is required by law or necessary to handle a legal claim, investigate fraud or protect people and our services.</li>
<li><strong>Business transactions:</strong> professional advisers and a successor in a merger, acquisition or transfer of the relevant business, subject to applicable protections and notice obligations.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell personal information. The software is not a shared marketing list for transportation companies. The specific restrictions on SMS consent and Google user data below also apply.</p>

<h2 id="cookies">8. Storage, website measurement and reCAPTCHA</h2>
<p>Our apps use browser storage and service-worker caches to support sign-in, preferences and offline application resources. Removing local storage can sign you out or reset local choices; it does not itself delete server-side records. Providers may use their own cookies or storage for the features they deliver.</p>
<p>Our own website measurement records the public page, referring website, campaign labels and the type of booking, phone or email click. It does not record form entries, clicked contact details, payment details or booking contents. A booking-link click does not establish that a reservation was completed. For advertising click identifiers, it records the supplying platform rather than the identifier itself. Measurement events are kept for 90 days with scheduled cleanup.</p>
<p>This measurement uses a random identifier in the browser tab's session storage, with a new session after 30 minutes of inactivity. It does not use an analytics cookie, persistent visitor identifier or device fingerprinting. We respect Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control for this measurement. You can <a href="/?koast_tracking=off">turn it off for this browser tab's session</a>. Other services, including a separately hosted booking provider, may have their own practices.</p>
<p><strong>reCAPTCHA.</strong> Protected sign-in and account flows use Google's reCAPTCHA for security, fraud and abuse prevention. That service processes device and interaction signals and may set a necessary security cookie. The short notice on those screens identifies that protection; hiding the floating badge does not disable the security check.</p>

<h2 id="sms">9. SMS and other communications</h2>
<p><strong>Koast Ride Updates is optional.</strong> We use a mobile number for recurring transactional text messages only after the number's owner gives express consent through our services. Consent is not a condition of purchase. Messages may include booking and quote notices, chauffeur assignment or arrival updates, pickup reminders, trip or flight changes, cancellation notices, payment and receipt notices, and support replies. Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out or HELP for help. See our <a href="/sms-terms">SMS Terms</a>.</p>
<p>We do not sell, rent or share mobile numbers, SMS opt-in data or SMS consent with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes. We may disclose this information to service providers, mobile carriers and vendors only as needed to deliver and support the messaging program, or when required by law; those parties may not use it for their own marketing. Opting out of text messages does not affect non-SMS communications needed to provide a requested service. A sign-in or verification code you request is separate from enrollment in recurring ride updates.</p>
<p>You may manage available notification settings and unsubscribe from promotional email using its instructions. Necessary account-security, reservation or business communications may still be sent through an appropriate channel.</p>

<h2 id="google-calendar">10. Google sign-in and Calendar</h2>
<p>Google sign-in provides the identity information needed to authenticate your Koast account. Calendar connection is a separate optional authorization. Where you connect Calendar, the permissions may allow reading calendar and event information and creating or updating events. Depending on the product and feature, this can include event titles, times, locations and availability, and calendar entries for your rides.</p>
<p>We use Google user data to provide the calendar features you enable: showing schedules, identifying scheduling conflicts, suggesting or timing pickups and keeping ride events up to date. We follow the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements. We do not use Google user data for advertising, sell it, transfer it to data brokers or use it to build advertising profiles. Human access is restricted to the circumstances permitted by that policy, such as your affirmative agreement, security purposes or legal obligations.</p>
<p>Koast stores authorizations and processes relevant event information so the connected features can work. Where an AI-assisted calendar feature is available, relevant information may be processed to answer the calendar request. Access and transfers must remain limited to the authorized user-facing feature and the applicable Limited Use requirements.</p>
<p>You can disconnect using the available Calendar settings or remove Koast from your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google account permissions</a>. Disconnecting stops Koast's ongoing access through the connection. Stored connection credentials are removed as disconnection is completed; provider revocation or cleanup may finish afterward. Removing a connection does not necessarily remove ride events already written to your calendar. Contact us if you need help. Rider account deactivation also stops its connected calendar syncing.</p>

<h2 id="retention-security">11. Retention and security</h2>
<p>Where you give a booking or payment authorization, we retain relevant acceptance records, including the accepting person and their authority, the company and account covered, designated payment-method references, the version and content of accepted terms and pricing or ride-policy schedules, selected scope and limits, supporting service requests, and later changes or withdrawal. These records help establish which bookings and payments were authorized. Accepting a standing booking/payment authorization does not provide consent for marketing messages, optional recording, device tracking or future cross-operator profile sharing.</p>
<p>We retain information for the time needed to provide the relevant service, support security and dispute handling, maintain required business and transaction records, and meet legal obligations. The period depends on the information, its purpose, active reservations or business relationships, and any applicable preservation requirement. The specific website-measurement and recording windows above apply to those features; they are not a retention period for every record. We delete or deidentify information when its permitted purposes no longer require identification.</p>
<p>We use safeguards including HTTPS, infrastructure security, authentication, organization-scoped access and encryption for supported stored data. Safeguards vary by feature, and no system can guarantee absolute security. If an incident requires notice, we provide it as required by applicable law. Information is processed in the United States and may be processed in other locations where our providers operate, subject to applicable requirements.</p>

<h2 id="account-deletion">12. Account deactivation, recovery and deletion</h2>
<p>The Rider app provides two separate choices under Settings → Security. Both require identity verification and deliberate confirmation.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Deactivate with 90-day recovery:</strong> access is disabled and existing sign-in sessions end. Data needed for recovery is retained for up to 90 days, with the deadline shown in the confirmation. A verified restoration request is required; signing in alone does not restore the account. Old passwords and sessions remain invalid. If not restored, the account proceeds to permanent deletion after the recovery period. Deactivation is not completed deletion.</li>
<li><strong>Request permanent deletion now:</strong> starts account and associated personal-data deletion without the optional 90-day hold. We disable access, verify and process the request, provide its status and confirm completion. Processing is not necessarily instantaneous. A completed permanent deletion cannot be undone.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>All users can contact us.</strong> Email <a href="mailto:reserve@koastride.com?subject=Koast%20privacy%20request">reserve@koastride.com</a> to request access, correction or deletion, including if you use Driver or Connect or cannot access the app. For Rider deletion, you can use the subject <em>Koast account deletion</em> without reinstalling the app or first selecting deactivation. We may verify your identity and authority. Do not email a password, sign-in code or full payment-card number. We help coordinate requests involving an operator's records as needed.</p>
<p>Closing an account does not cancel a reservation, request a refund or waive a payment obligation. Limited reservation, transaction, receipt, security or other records may remain where needed for outstanding services, legal and tax requirements, fraud prevention or legal claims. Retained data is restricted to those purposes. An optional recovery choice does not extend an applicable legal deadline. Removing a staff member's access does not automatically delete the company's business records.</p>

<h2 id="rights">13. Your choices and privacy rights</h2>
<p>You can update available profile details, change supported permissions and notification settings, disconnect optional services and contact us with a privacy request. Depending on your location and the laws that apply, you may have rights to access or obtain a copy of personal information, correct inaccuracies, request deletion, opt out of certain disclosures or uses, limit certain uses of sensitive information, or appeal a response. We handle applicable rights requests without unlawful discrimination and may need to verify identity or an authorized agent's authority.</p>
<p>California residents may have rights under California privacy law where applicable, including knowing the categories, sources, uses and disclosures of information, correction and deletion, and opting out of sale or sharing for cross-context behavioral advertising. We do not sell personal information or use our own website measurement for cross-context behavioral advertising. Contact us about a request or an applicable right; we will explain any lawful exception rather than treating every record as deletable.</p>
<p>The services are intended for adult account holders. An adult may arrange authorized transportation for a child, and we process the passenger details needed for that booking. If you believe a child supplied account information without appropriate authorization, contact us.</p>

<h2 id="changes-contact">14. Changes and contact</h2>
<p>We post revisions with an updated date and provide additional notice for material changes where required. A material new use or optional feature may require a separate choice. Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:reserve@koastride.com">reserve@koastride.com</a>, Krujim Inc doing business as Koast, San Francisco, California. Related agreements are available in our <a href="/legal/">Legal center</a>.</p>
